      "final_text": "Done. `check_candidate` returns `VERIFIED` for all five requirements, and `verify_passport` reproduces it.\n\n**Fix** (only [candidate/Solution.lean](<workspace>/candidate/Solution.lean) changed): `VyperSqrt.sqrt` is now the deployed loop with the PR 4486 correction \u2014 `vyperSqrtWith fun y z => if y < z then y else z`, i.e. the smaller of the last two iterates instead of always the last one. That turns the Babylonian loop's round-to-nearest behavior into round-down: on raw 9999999998 it now returns the floor root rather than 9999999999.\n\n**Proof sketch**: the loop on Nat values is Newton iteration `N(z) = (A/z + z)/2` for `A = a\u00b710\u00b9\u2070`. Seed `a/2 + 5\u00b710\u2079 \u2265 \u221aA` (AM-GM via `four_mul_le_sq`); iterates stay in decimal range (`step_bound`, using `A/y \u2264 s` above the root and `\u2264 s+2` at it, plus closed `decide` bounds); the halving bound drives the error to \u2264 2 within fuel, one quadratic step reaches `{s, s+1}`, and `min_newton_eq_sqrt` plus the fixed-point lemma identify the minimum as `Nat.sqrt A`. The five theorems follow by casting (`Nat.sqrt_le`, `Nat.lt_succ_sqrt`).\n\n**Verification**: `lean_build` clean (no errors, no `sorry`); official check `VERIFIED` across all six kernels with permitted axioms only; executable property tests pass (2001 cases); passport `.proofforge/passport-001.json` (`ed45b6db\u2026`) reproduced.",
